  "user_scenario": "You are Daniel Ibarra, a 39-year-old high-school chemistry teacher in Portland who is patient but likes to understand what he is paying for. You have an individual Cascade vision plan. On September 10 you went to Lindstrom Eye Associates for your yearly eye exam and, because your two eyes have drifted far apart, Dr. Lindstrom did a specialty contact-lens fitting and evaluation for you. The exam has already been settled, but a statement from the practice still shows the fitting as waiting on Cascade, and the front desk told you they will bill you whatever Cascade says is yours. You are calling to have Cascade decide the fitting and tell you what you owe for it, and you are happy for the representative to record that decision for you today. You open by giving your name and saying you are calling from 5035550119.\n\nYou hand over details only as they are asked for. When the representative needs to confirm who you are, you give your date of birth, 1987-02-11, and your ZIP code, 97211; if they need more, you can read the member ID on your card, CM7358216, or give your email, daniel.ibarra@cascadiamail.net. If the representative asks about other coverage, you say you have no other vision insurance; only if they ask specifically do you mention that your dental plan is also with Cascade on the same account and that you bought a Smile & Sight savings membership in January.\n\nYou do not know what the plan pays for a fitting and you do not offer a number. If the representative brings up the lenses you ordered afterwards, you explain that you ordered the lenses Dr. Lindstrom prescribed from Kearney Contact Lens Direct, an online supplier, on September 18 and paid them yourself, and that the supplier said it would send Cascade the receipt with the doctor's note about your eyes; you have not filed anything yourself. When the representative tells you that receipt has to be filed first and hands the filing to you, you file it yourself for the amount they tell you and read out the confirmation you get back. When the representative tells you the fitting decision is recorded and what your share of the fitting is, you thank them and end the call.",
